The objections to this {su'a} idea is that it's trying to express a logical=
 distinction by searching through the dictionary to find words with vaguely=
 relevant glosses (such as "particular"), finding some discourse markers gl=
ossed in that way, and arbitrarily inventing new uses for those discourse m=
arkers in the hope that they will magically express the desired meaning. It=
's the {da'i} bollocks all over again.

